  <cell width="340">
   <color r="255" g="248" b="178"><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10">
    In Challenge and Campaign mode the Porbeagle will be available when your zoo has reached 5 stars. 
   </font></color>
<p /><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10"> The Porbeagle (Lamna nasus) is a shark form the mackerel sharks (Lamnidae).
</font><p /><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10"> The maximum length is 11 ft. (3.50 m.) The heaviest Probeagle weight about 550 lb. (250 kg.) His big black eyes, the pionted snout and the little sharp teeth are real eyecatchers.  The upperside of the Porbeagle is dark grey, the bottom is white.
</font><p /><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10"> This sharkspecies lives seperately or in shoals and hunts on small shoals of deep sea fish, other sharks and squid. The resistance is very low, it takes about 14 years to dubble the population.
</font><p /><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10"> The Porbeagle lives in the Atlantic Ocean, the Mediteranean sea, from the southwest to southeast of the Pacific Ocean ans the Indian Ocean.
</font><p /><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10"> The Porbeagle is wanted by commercial fishermen and is caught for fun. The meat is used for human consumption: oil and cattlefood. The fins are used for sharkfinsoup. The meat can be roasted or grilled
</font><p /><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10"> The Probeagle is seen as a potential danger to divers, because of their size and activities. But there are rarely attacks on humans or boats. This animal can be of harm to humans, but is not deadly.

 
</font></cell>
